#!/usr/bin/env bash

DOCKER_VERSION=$(docker -v | cut -d " " -f 3 | tr "," " ")
NGINX_VERSION=$(nginx  -v 2>&1 | cut -d " " -f 3 | cut -d "/" -f 2)
OSUname=$(uname)

#The following command is used to send the mail to target email id (This require's configuration of mail )
#cat <<EOF | mail -s "$(date): Report on $(hostname)" "developer198622@gmail.com"

cat <<EOF
Docker version: $DOCKER_VERSION
Nginx Version: $NGINX_VERSION
OS uname: $OSUname
EOF



cd /lib/modules/`uname -r`

In the above line `uname -r` print's the current version of the kernel

This modules include's the device driver's, File systems (ext4,xfs,btrfs), Network protocols,Virtualization modules,Security modules.

sudo modprobe iwlwifi --> where it load's the module for the wireless detection 

[/lib/modules/$(uname -r)/kernel/drivers/net/wireless] The above command is used load this module.

